### API configuration

Every key the API reads, and nothing else. A test (`apps/api/src/config/env.schema.spec.ts`)
fails if this block, `apps/api/.env.example`, `apps/api/.env.ci` and the code disagree.

<!-- env:api:start -->

```bash
# apps/api/.env
# PostgreSQL connection string (docker-compose.yml locally, `fly postgres attach` when deployed)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://app:app@localhost:5432/app
# development | test | staging | production; staging and production log JSON lines
NODE_ENV=development
# Port the API listens on (optional, default 3000)
PORT=3000
# Comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the API (optional, default none)
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
# Sentry DSN (optional; empty disables error reporting)
SENTRY_DSN=
# Lowest log level written: verbose | debug | log | warn | error | fatal (optional, default log)
LOG_LEVEL=log
```

<!-- env:api:end -->
{% endif %}
## Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `pnpm verify` | What CI runs, locally, for the packages changed since `origin/main` (lint, format, doctor and audit always cover the whole repo). Runs automatically before every push. |
| `pnpm verify --all` | Everything CI runs, for every package |
| `pnpm doctor` | Harness health: rules without enforcers, expired exceptions, blocking gaps, backlog. |
| `pnpm lint` / `pnpm typecheck` / `pnpm test` / `pnpm build` | One gate at a time |
| `pnpm e2e` | Builds the apps and walks the critical journeys (first time: `pnpm -r --workspace-concurrency=1 --if-present e2e:install`). Another checkout running at the same time: set `E2E_PORT` (web, default 4173) / `E2E_MOBILE_PORT` (mobile, default 8082) |
| `pnpm format` | Prettier over the repo |

## Deploy
{% if 'api' in apps %}
The API deploys to Fly.io staging on every green push to `main`. One-time setup:

1. `brew install flyctl && fly auth login`
2. `fly launch --no-deploy --config apps/api/fly.staging.toml` (creates the app and its Postgres)
3. Set each key from the API configuration block: `fly secrets set KEY=value --config apps/api/fly.staging.toml`
4. `fly tokens create deploy --config apps/api/fly.staging.toml` and save it as the GitHub secret
   `FLY_API_TOKEN` (repo → Settings → Secrets → Actions)
{% endif %}
{%- if 'web' in apps or 'site' in apps %}
Web and site: connect the repo to Vercel (or any static host) with the build command and output
directory from each app's `package.json`.
{%- endif %}
{%- if 'mobile' in apps %}
Mobile: `pnpm --filter ./apps/mobile exec eas build --profile preview` (needs `eas login`).
{%- endif %}

